-- title:
--   Ordinary eigenline at p=3, weights 2 ≤ k ≤ 4
-- statement:
--   Fix the prime $p$ with $p \neq 2$ and $p = 3$, a level $N \geq 1$ with $p \nmid N$, a finite set $S$ of natural numbers with $p \notin S$, and a weight $k \in \mathbb{Z}$ with $2 \le k \le p+1$, together with a natural number $kn$ whose image in $\mathbb{Z}$ is $k$. Let $F$ be a field of characteristic $p$ and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism to $F$ from `heckeAlgebra N k S`, the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_k(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$, and $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$, $q \notin S$; assume $\theta(T_p) \neq 0$. Let $\rho : \operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(F)$ be a homomorphism (on the automorphism group of `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` over $\mathbb{Q}$) which is trivial on the subgroup fixing some finite-dimensional intermediate field pointwise, and which is irreducible in the sense that for every nonzero $u \in F^2$ some $\sigma$ moves $u$ out of the line $F \cdot u$. Assume that for every prime $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$, $\ell \neq p$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $A$, and every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ and inducing $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field of $A$, one has $\operatorname{tr} \rho(\sigma) = \theta(T_\ell)$ and $\det \rho(\sigma) = \ell^{kn-1}$ in $F$. Let $P$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $P$. Then, first, for all such $\ell$, $A$ and $\sigma$ the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ equals $X^2 - \theta(T_\ell) X + \ell^{kn-1}$; and secondly there is a nonzero $v \in F^2$ such that $F \cdot v$ is stable under $\rho(\sigma)$ for all $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $P$; $\rho(\sigma)w - w \in F \cdot v$ for all $w \in F^2$ and all $\sigma$ in the image in $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ of the inertia subgroup of $P$; $\rho(\sigma)w - \theta(T_p)\, w \in F \cdot v$ for all $w$ whenever $\sigma$ lies in the decomposition subgroup of $P$ and induces $x \mapsto x^{p}$ on the residue field; and $\rho(\sigma) v = a^{kn-1} v$ whenever $\sigma$ is in that inertia image and $a \in \mathbb{N}$ satisfies $\sigma\mu = \mu^a$ for all $p$-th roots of unity $\mu$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$.
--
--   This is the $p = 3$ case of the statement, due in essence to Deligne, that a mod $p$ representation attached to a Hecke eigensystem with non-zero $T_p$-eigenvalue is ordinary at $p$: it carries a decomposition-stable line on which inertia at $p$ acts through the $(k-1)$-st power of the mod $p$ cyclotomic character, with unramified Frobenius eigenvalue $\theta(T_p)$ on the quotient. It feeds the determination of the local shape at $3$ of such representations, [`GaloisRep.deligneOrdinaryShape_of_theta_T_ne_zero_of_det_eq_pow_of_eq_three`](thm.html#GaloisRep.deligneOrdinaryShape_of_theta_T_ne_zero_of_det_eq_pow_of_eq_three).
